title: 'Correction: Gnomon is a localhost GUI (terminal-like), not an in-terminal TUI'
summary: |-
  The founder clarified that Gnomon is a full GUI tool that feels terminal-like, running on localhost in the browser and possibly as a desktop app later. It is not an in-terminal TUI. That corrects the reading of P8-D26 and D32 (pi-tui as the shell renderer).

  Other founder decisions in this exchange:
  - CLI only; no full in-terminal UI.
  - Persona voice based on Simplified Technical English.
  - No restyling pass; brief by instruction.

  Spec v3.2 is needed for the localhost GUI shell. It must cover localhost web security: origin lock, token, and DNS-rebinding protection.
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
decisions:
  - id: P8-D50
    decision: Gnomon's shell is a terminal-like GUI served by the local kernel on localhost and opened in the browser (desktop wrapper optional later); supersedes the in-terminal reading of P8-D26 and P8-D32
    rationale: 'Founder: "i was under the notion that we were building a full gui tool that could be just browser or as a desktop app eventualy" and "i was under the belief this would always just be running on localhost"'
  - id: P8-D51
    decision: CLI only for the terminal (gnomon spawn/status/approve/replay); no full in-terminal UI
    rationale: Founder choice.
  - id: P8-D52
    decision: Default persona voice follows Simplified Technical English (ASD-STE100) style rules with a length budget; no restyling pass, brevity by instruction
    rationale: 'Founder: "no restyling, brief sounds fine and fair people are wanting for that STE type speak"'
